.TH USB-BACKUP-CLI 1 "2026" "USB Backup" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
usb-backup-cli \- verified, encrypted backups to registered USB disks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B usb-backup-cli
.I command
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B usb-backup-cli
makes a verified zip of every source folder on the USB disk whose turn it is
(the registered disk that was used longest ago), encrypted with age
(post-quantum) when keys exist. Old period folders are only deleted after
every new archive was verified.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Back up all source folders
.RB ( \-\-target ", " \-\-any\-disk ", " \-\-tag ", " \-\-force ", " \-\-wait ", " \-\-dry\-run ", " \-\-quiet\-skip ", " \-\-json ).
.TP
.B verify
Check backups again; \fB\-\-all\fR for every folder; with \fB\-\-identity\fR or \fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR also decrypt and unpack.
.TP
.B list
Browse periods, sources and files
.RB ( \-\-week ", " \-\-tag ", " \-\-path ", " \-\-search ).
.TP
.B restore
Restore files (\fB\-\-tag\fR, \fB\-\-week\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR, \fB\-\-to\fR or \fB\-\-original\fR). Existing files are never overwritten.
.TP
.B status
Connected backup disks: health, free space, folders, last backup.
.TP
.B enroll \fIdisk\fR \-\-name \fINAME\fR
Register a disk (vault password).
.TP
.BR disks ", " forget " \fIname\fR"
Show or remove registrations.
.TP
.B keys init|passwd|rotate|rewrap|status
Manage the keys.
.TP
.B config show|set|add\-source|remove\-source|import|export
Manage the settings (signed by the operator).
.TP
.B install|uninstall
Start a backup when a registered disk is plugged in (udev rule), or stop doing that.
.TP
.BR eject ", " version ", " help
.SH PASSWORDS
Passwords are never taken from arguments or environment variables: use
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR or the prompt.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 success with warnings; 2 no backup disk; 3 wrong disk for this
period; 4 skipped (recently done); 5 another backup is running; 6 unknown
disk; 7 settings or registrations changed without the operator; 10 disk
check failed; 11 read or write error; 12 verification failed; 13 decryption
or re-wrap failed; 64 wrong usage.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/usb-backup/
(as root) or
.I ~/.config/usb-backup/
: settings, registrations, public keys, log.
